course: dictionary
lesson: 8727
title: One word, two meanings: sept
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sept has more than one meaning, so context decides which one you need. Look at the words around it and at how it is written. «Sept.» with a capital S and a full stop is a short form, so it usually points to a date or a calendar.
explain: On a calendar or form, «Sept.» is the short form of September, the ninth month of the year. Write it in a date, such as 5 Sept., and every reader knows the month. Without the full stop and capital, the word could be a different sort of word.
explain: In history, a sept is a branch of a clan or family, especially in Ireland and Scotland. In «a sept of the clan», the word clan is the clue. A clan is a big family group, so a sept is one smaller branch inside it.
explain: Always ask: what does the sentence want? A date needs the month, and a clan needs a family group. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: «Sept.» is the short form of September, the ninth month of the year.
fact: A sept is a branch of a clan or family, especially in Ireland and Scotland.
fact: The clue word clan tells you that sept means a family group in history.
fact: In French number words, «quatre-vingt-dix-sept» is a hidden sum that means 97.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word you need, so check the words around it.
exercise: On a calendar you see «Sept.» next to a date. What does Sept. mean? | *September, the ninth month | A kind of food | A branch of a clan | Hiking boots
exercise: «Quatre-vingt-dix-sept is a hidden sum: quatre × vingt + dix + sept = 4 × 20 + 10 + 7 = 97.» What does the sum add up to? | 74 | 27 | 47 | *97
exercise: «A sept of the clan» is a branch of a family group. Which word in the phrase is the clue to its meaning? | sept | the | of | *clan
test: Which is a correct short form of the month September? | Sepr | *Sept. | Setember | Sembr
test: In «a sept of the clan», what is a sept? | *A branch of a family group | A grey, wet day | A type of ship | A month of the year
exam: Which meaning fits «a sept of the clan»? | A type of petrol station | The ninth month of the year | *A branch of a family group | A grey, wet day
